Make the escaping of `{{ name }}` settable per template.

crow::mustache::template_t::escape is private and always HTML-escapes
(& < > " ' / ` =). flAPI renders SQL with the same engine, where HTML
entities are wrong: '{{ name }}' with O'Brien became 'O&#39;Brien' and
{{ conn.path }} rendered /data as &#x2F;data. flAPI also renders an HTML
page (Swagger UI) with it, which must keep HTML escaping.

This adds a public escape_function (a plain function pointer), a static
template_t::html_escape (the old body, unchanged), and set_escape() /
get_escape(). The default stays html_escape, so every existing caller renders
exactly as before. Partials and lambda results rendered by a template inherit
its escape function.

Not yet submitted upstream (https://github.com/CrowCpp/crow).

